00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:41.783
- Your hair!

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:46.903
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:50.650
We're gonna have to talk
about your hair for a minute.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.379
- You realize when I...
I just screamed that

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:55.069
(laughter)

00:00:55.069 --> 00:00:58.530
when I was in Australia, I did her show,

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.390
when I was with them! Yeah!

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.130
We were all in Australia, I did your show,

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.450
and it was so weird to be

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.650
on zoom that far away from you.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.940
So it's so nice to be...

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:07.963
- So you play Satan.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.353
- Yeah, Satan.

00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:12.350
- What does one do for
research for that role?

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.550
Just, do you read the Bible? Or...

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.910
- No, I didn't read.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:16.833
No. I did read that!

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:19.349
I did look at the demonic book that,

00:01:19.349 --> 00:01:21.550
that we referenced this book.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.780
So I did a deep dive.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.920
Cause there's like all these
different words for Satan,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:26.753
so I looked up...

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.586
- Like Lucifer, all those things

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.183
- DDD. Demonic deep dive.

00:01:30.069 --> 00:01:31.610
- Beelzebub, I think there's a lot of 'em.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.630
- There is a lot! Right?

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.950
And so, but I don't know if you're playing

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.940
somebody that's so evil,

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.270
I don't think evil
people think they're evil

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.230
or they're bad.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.210
Right? They think kind
of think they're good.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.140
And so...

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.461
- I think they're called
narcissists, but yeah.

00:01:45.461 --> 00:01:46.490
(laughter)

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.323
- We see them all the time

00:01:47.323 --> 00:01:48.156
- All the time!

00:01:48.156 --> 00:01:49.280
- They're just out and about.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.370
- So I don't know.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.840
I wanted her to be a little bit like

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.770
Tracy Flick in "Election".

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:54.603
- Yeah.

00:01:54.603 --> 00:01:57.540
- And I think she desperately
wants like friends.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:01.480
I think she's obsessed with,
I think she really feels

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.330
like she's gonna get Melissa on her side.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.301
She's like, she's like, I could see it.

00:02:05.301 --> 00:02:06.134
- Probably.

00:02:06.134 --> 00:02:09.480
- And I think she just really wants to be,

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.110
like picked for the team.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.700
And I don't think she ever is.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.406
- And then burn you alive.

00:02:14.406 --> 00:02:15.848
- And then burn you alive!

00:02:15.848 --> 00:02:17.839
- But with a smile!

00:02:17.839 --> 00:02:18.982
- She'll turn on you really fast.

00:02:18.982 --> 00:02:20.219
- That was a great movie.

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:21.517
Yeah. Can I get you something?

00:02:21.517 --> 00:02:22.624
Yeah. Burn you alive.

00:02:22.624 --> 00:02:24.380
Light the couch on fire.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.610
- I just think that'd be a more,

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.350
like a more fun role to play.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.980
- It's so fun and these
guys let you do anything,

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.800
they're so fun to work
for because don't like,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.480
they let you try, anything, right?

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.859
- Just we don't have a plan going in.

00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:39.909
- Yes you do!

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:41.080
- They're just like do something.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:41.913
- No, I love that.

00:02:41.913 --> 00:02:43.290
But do you think that
y'all do that because you

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.280
are those kind of actors,
you like a little bit of,

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.240
I mean your whole life is improv,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.160
I think, your children would say.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.450
- I have to say when you have, I mean,

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.980
when Ben and I, think when you have like,

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:54.813
people like this,

00:02:54.813 --> 00:02:56.340
and we have such a great cast.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.438
- Yeah.

00:02:57.438 --> 00:02:58.920
- It's like, here's the roadmap, but like

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.660
you don't hire great people and be like

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.230
don't do what you do.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.323
Yeah.

00:03:03.323 --> 00:03:04.730
- It's very fun, like
going on set and like going

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:07.460
through a scene that you're
gonna go in the next day.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.990
And then like hopping on and then going,

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:10.993
like rehearsing?

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:12.930
It's so ridiculous.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:13.763
- Yeah, it is.

00:03:13.763 --> 00:03:16.334
- Because you, like, you
get halfway through it

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:17.323
and you would just start talking.

00:03:19.776 --> 00:03:21.450
- Welcome to my life, Kevin.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.517
- I know. It must be terrible.

00:03:23.517 --> 00:03:24.665
- It would just change,

00:03:24.665 --> 00:03:25.994
the whole scene would be a different scene

00:03:25.994 --> 00:03:26.827
but it was be like,

00:03:26.827 --> 00:03:27.660
that's good.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.390
- So you, Kevin, you played Ben's dad.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.880
So do you think that he'd
make a pretty good son?

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:34.670
No pressure in answering, he's right here.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.073
- He was a fine son.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.240
And we covered a lot
of ground in the sauna.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.343
- [Ben] We did.

00:03:42.343 --> 00:03:44.130
- Yeah. It was so fun.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.657
I mean, just when we were
talking about setting it up

00:03:46.657 --> 00:03:49.613
and when Ben mentioned
it, when he called me,

00:03:49.613 --> 00:03:51.080
it's just an odd thing.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.050
I had just finished building a sauna

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.756
or was in the throws of...

00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:56.080
- Did you say you built a sauna?

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.290
- Yeah. That was my
Covid project because...

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.683
- Okay. I just love how you
were just like, oh yeah,

00:04:00.683 --> 00:04:01.516
and then I built a sauna.

00:04:01.516 --> 00:04:03.424
Like that was very flippant.

00:04:03.424 --> 00:04:04.897
- [Melissa] The odds are that are like,

00:04:04.897 --> 00:04:05.730
they're so crazy.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.563
- It was so weird,
cause it was like, yeah,

00:04:06.563 --> 00:04:07.600
I'm doing this thing.

00:04:08.451 --> 00:04:10.420
And you know, you play my dad and you,

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.860
and we sit in the sauna and talk.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:15.840
And I said, you know what
I was just doing today?

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.650
I was hooking up the
heater, the final heater to

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.490
the sauna because there was nothing to do.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.760
I was, there was no work.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.893
We were locked down and
my wife was like, wow.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:28.915
- [Kelly] You need to do something.

00:04:28.915 --> 00:04:30.380
- She had bought me a book about

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.550
building a Finnish sauna and said...

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.200
- Not inside the house!

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.653
- Yeah. Outside. Yes. Outside. Out!

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:39.300
- So, yeah.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.100
- I feel very lazy. I didn't learn,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.570
I didn't build anything
nor did I learn a language.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.260
You built a sauna, and
the first time you said

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.420
Finnish sauna I was like,
like a finished project.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.820
And I was like, oh no,
he means like Finland.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:51.653
- The Finns.

00:04:51.653 --> 00:04:52.992
- Like the Finnish.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:53.825
- Yeah.

00:04:53.825 --> 00:04:55.260
- Oh my God, I thought
you, I thought you meant,

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.530
I went Tim 'The Toolman' Taylor,

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.880
I thought she was like, you
need to actually finish the job.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.590
Like I thought you went there to oh, okay,

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.423
like I finish.

00:05:02.423 --> 00:05:04.200
- As opposed to a, yeah.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.240
- What makes it Finnish in its
look, versus a normal sauna?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.307
Now I'm curious.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:11.010
- It's not just, it's
not what the look is,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.530
it's just how it's vented.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:13.363
- Ooh.

00:05:13.363 --> 00:05:14.196
- It's pretty basic.

00:05:14.196 --> 00:05:15.260
It's just, you know...

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.560
- The Finns, right?

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.512
- They're really great with venting.

00:05:19.512 --> 00:05:20.612
They know how to vent!

